# 🔴 SUPABASE CONNECTION DETAILS — a CREDENTIAL, and the most dangerous one this repo will ever sit
# next to. The database password and the service_role key give FULL read/write access to every
# school's data, bypassing row-level security entirely. This repo is PUBLIC: one `git add -A` and
# they are in the history for ever, exactly as the Google backup codes were (see below).
#
# Added 2026-10-09, BEFORE the file exists, so there is no window in which it is unprotected.
# `secrets/supabase.env.example` is the template and IS committed — it holds no values.
# `secrets/*` and not `secrets/` — git does not descend into an ignored DIRECTORY, so a rule on the
# folder makes the un-ignore below unreachable and the template uncommittable too. Caught by
# `git check-ignore` before either file existed.
secrets/*
!secrets/*.example
*.env
.env*
!*.env.example

# Google account backup codes — a CREDENTIAL. Was committed to this PUBLIC repo on 2026-06-22
# and removed 2026-08-27. Never put one here again; the file now lives outside the repo.
Backup codes.pdf
*ackup*code*

# The director's SIGNATURE and the certificate artwork. `Atom Signature.png` appeared in the repo
